From 122d019df2a8f2406cd98100eceab12e15f2ba9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Po-Han Huang <53919306+nvpohanh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:08:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] K3.1 session affinity: carry the agent context across the Python
 chat-processor hop; seed subagent groups from the parent

On --dyn-chat-processor sglang|vllm, RoutedEngine rebuilds the request context, so the typed
registry entries the HTTP layer set are lost. The cherry-picked upstream fix (ai-dynamo/dynamo#15333,
rebase of #12191) restores SessionAffinityId. This adds the same carry for AgentContext (the parent
session id) and makes an unbound subagent group start on its parent's worker:

- bindings: keep AgentContext on the Python Context and re-insert it into the routed request's
  registry. The request body (PreprocessedRequest.agent_context, i.e. the worker payload) is left
  unchanged, so workers receive exactly what they received before.
- migration / prefill router: re-insert the registry AgentContext where the per-attempt and the
  prefill sub-request contexts are rebuilt (both already re-insert SessionAffinityId).
- routing_host: group_binding_id falls back to the registry AgentContext; when the subagent group
  is unbound, its first selection is offered the parent session's current target on that hop
  (a hint: a failing seeded selection retries unseeded). Logs
  "K3.1 session affinity: subagent group seeded from parent session binding".

Campaign-local infrastructure shim on v1.6.0 (701da252); not filed upstream.

Signed-off-by: Po-Han Huang <53919306+nvpohanh@users.noreply.github.com>
